WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.500
Scientists tell how healthy rainforests are by listening to the sounds of their wildlife.
科学家通过听雨林中野生动物的声音，来判断雨林有多健康。

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:13.270
A healthy forest is alive with animal calls and birdsong but an unhealthy forest is much quieter.
健康的森林里充满了动物的叫声和鸟鸣，而不健康的森林则要安静得多。

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.740
However, that is a big job.
然而，这是一项大工程。

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:24.360
Researchers can make thousands of hours of recordings but then someone has to listen to them all and pick out the different animal and bird calls.
研究人员可以录下数千小时的声音，但接下来得有人把这些录音全部听一遍，并从中分辨出各种不同的动物叫声和鸟叫声。

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.200
What if that someone is an AI though?
不过，要是听录音的这个“人”是人工智能呢？

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.550
Scientists are using AI technology to help with the task.
科学家正在利用人工智能技术来帮助完成这项任务。

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:40.010
Through the new Forest Listeners web experiment, scientists want people around the world—including you—to help too.
通过新推出的“森林聆听者”网络实验，科学家希望包括你在内的世界各地的人也来帮忙。

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:45.290
The site gets you to move around a virtual forest, listening for wildlife.
这个网站让你在一片虚拟森林中四处走动，留心听野生动物的声音。

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:50.630
When you find a new species, you listen to its song until you can remember it.
发现一个新物种时，你就一直听它的叫声，直到能记住为止。

00:00:51.430 --> 00:01:02.300
The next step is to listen to real forest recordings (there are more than 1.2 million of them), and decide for each one whether you can hear that animal call, can’t hear it or aren’t sure.
下一步是听真实的森林录音（这样的录音超过120万条），并对每一条作出判断：你是能听到那种动物的叫声，听不到，还是不确定。

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:08.630
The answers people give are then used to train AI to identify animals by their sounds.
随后，人们给出的答案会用来训练人工智能根据声音识别动物。

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:13.750
Scientists say that the project helps them process a huge number of recordings.
科学家们说，这个项目帮助他们处理大量录音。

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:18.060
Without AI, it would take many years to study them all.
如果没有人工智能，要把这些录音全部研究一遍，得花上很多年。

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:24.430
“Every sound tagged by a forest listener helps train our AI models,” the scientists said.
科学家们说：“森林聆听者标注的每一个声音，都有助于训练我们的人工智能模型。”

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:32.630
“This group effort provides us with valuable information, allowing us to notice small changes in species’ presence and behavior.
“大家的这份共同努力为我们提供了宝贵的信息，让我们能够注意到物种在出没和行为上的细微变化。

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:36.460
These are important signs of how healthy a forest is.”
这些是反映森林健康状况的重要迹象。”
